# Translations
# `locale/**/*.mo` is deliberately NOT ignored — it stays committed alongside the
# `.po` it is compiled from. This project has no build hook that runs
# `compilemessages` on `pip install`, so an editable/source-checkout install (the
# thing a contributor and a downstream packager both do) would ship with no working
# Arabic until someone remembered a separate step. `pyproject.toml` also force-includes
# `*.mo` into the wheel via `artifacts`, independent of this file, so a later change
# here can't silently break translations in a *built* package either way. See
# docs/internationalization.md.

